WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.266
(city sounds, subway train squeal)

00:00:05.163 --> 00:00:09.396
- [Narrator] One spring afternoon in 2015,

00:00:09.396 --> 00:00:12.539
I decided to visit the world in a day.

00:00:12.539 --> 00:00:15.469
New York opens itself up to
those willing to explore it,

00:00:15.469 --> 00:00:17.784
and so the view from
elsewhere can be glimpsed

00:00:17.784 --> 00:00:21.284
and enjoyed by wandering the city streets.

00:00:22.541 --> 00:00:25.108
I want to witness all
across the city how people

00:00:25.108 --> 00:00:27.315
take their home country
with them to New York

00:00:27.315 --> 00:00:31.482
and adapt easily or uneasily
to this challenging metropolis.

00:00:33.751 --> 00:00:36.598
I want to see how people long
for home, I want to observe

00:00:36.598 --> 00:00:39.879
how they declare "this is my home."

00:00:39.879 --> 00:00:42.736
For as long as I can
remember, I've been a walker,

00:00:42.736 --> 00:00:45.983
one who makes sense of the
world by strolling through it.

00:00:45.983 --> 00:00:48.176
Many immigrants from
countries where the walker

00:00:48.176 --> 00:00:50.865
has not been displaced by
the automobile lay claim

00:00:50.865 --> 00:00:54.524
to the city by grasping it
underfoot, they warm up to it

00:00:54.524 --> 00:00:58.256
at walking pace, so I walk
to connect with the city,

00:00:58.256 --> 00:01:02.001
but also to connect with other
immigrants who pursue home.

00:01:02.001 --> 00:01:05.335
Step by step, encounter by encounter,

00:01:05.335 --> 00:01:08.252
ambition by ambition, the way I do.

00:01:13.593 --> 00:01:16.926
(light electric guitar)

00:01:25.595 --> 00:01:29.762
(upbeat jazzy music)

